427
00:41:05,800 --> 00:41:11,680
dreamlike and hallucinatory atmosphere. The novel not only reviews the official history of Mexico, but  

428
00:41:11,680 --> 00:41:17,320
subjects it to the critical gaze of imagination and memory, proposing fiction as a  

429
00:41:17,320 --> 00:41:23,440
form of resistance and search for justice. Beyond her narrative, Garro was one of the  

430
00:41:23,440 --> 00:41:29,320
Mexico's most influential playwrights, renewing the theater with pieces such as Un hogar sólido,  

431
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:35,040
The tree and The lady on her balcony, where the borders between reality and illusion, past and  

432
00:41:35,040 --> 00:41:42,080
