00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:13,520
from motherhood to violence, from political memory to desire. 

449
00:43:13,520 --> 00:43:17,960
These writers have not only conquered the literary space. They have also reached the  

450
00:43:17,960 --> 00:43:23,680
large audiences, have won important awards, have convinced critics and, above all,  

451
00:43:25,080 --> 00:43:30,640
They have won over readers. And they have done so with very different styles and voices, often  

452
00:43:30,640 --> 00:43:36,520
moving away from labels and looking for new ways to say what was not said before. 

453
00:43:36,520 --> 00:43:42,200
Today, literature written by women is a plural, free and constantly evolving territory.  

454
00:43:42,200 --> 00:43:45,960
transformation. There are writers who explore memory and history,  

455
